---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const domains = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'Research and learning',
    problem: 'AI can make reading, synthesis and explanation faster without necessarily improving judgment or understanding.',
    test: 'Use real papers and arguments, then check what can still be explained, challenged and defended with less assistance.',
    signal: 'Better source judgment, clearer reasoning and stronger unaided explanation.',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Software engineering',
    problem: 'AI can produce code faster than a person can understand the architecture, risks and failure modes behind it.',
    test: 'Use AI on real engineering work, then test whether design choices, failures and critical code can still be explained and reviewed independently.',
    signal: 'Better debugging, stronger code review, clearer architecture decisions and less dependence on opaque generated code.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Engineering leadership',
    problem: 'Faster output does not automatically improve prioritization, delegation, communication or judgment under uncertainty.',
    test: 'Use AI to rehearse decisions, reviews and difficult scenarios, then compare predictions with what actually happens.',
    signal: 'Clearer trade-offs, fewer avoidable reversals and better decisions in real work.',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    title: 'Nemosyne / Moneta',
    problem: 'AI can accelerate experimentation so quickly that implementation may outrun human understanding.',
    test: 'Use AI freely to explore possibilities, then reconstruct and test the parts that become important enough to keep.',
    signal: 'A system that remains understandable, testable and maintainable while still benefiting from fast exploration.',
  },
];

const steps = [
  ['Find the real bottleneck', 'Ask what is actually preventing better work or better understanding.'],
  ['Use the abundance', 'Apply AI, existing knowledge, software, data or other available resources to that bottleneck.'],
  ['Do real work', 'Test the idea inside work that already matters rather than creating artificial exercises where possible.'],
  ['Check what remains', 'Reduce the assistance and see whether understanding, judgment or performance has actually improved.'],
];
---
<Layout
  title="Practice"
  description="Agalmic Research experiments with whether AI can increase durable human capability, not just make output faster."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Practice</p>
      <h1>Can AI make people more capable, not just more productive?</h1>
      <p class="lede">This part of Agalmic Research uses real work as a testbed. The question is simple: when AI makes a task easier, does the person become better able to understand, judge and perform that work, or merely better able to produce an answer with help?</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">The distinction</p>
      <blockquote>Faster output is not the same thing as stronger capability.</blockquote>
      <p>If the goal is learning or judgment, the useful test is what remains after some of the assistance is removed. Can the person explain the result, spot errors, make a decision, solve a related problem or rebuild the important part?</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Current areas</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Where we are testing this idea.</h2>
          <p>The experiments are attached to work that already matters rather than treated as a generic self-improvement programme.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        {domains.map((item) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class="card-kicker">{item.n}</span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p><strong>The problem:</strong> {item.problem}</p>
            <p><strong>How we test it:</strong> {item.test}</p>
            <p><strong>A useful sign:</strong> {item.signal}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Using AI well</p>
        <h2>Explore quickly. Understand what you keep.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">AI is especially useful for widening the search space: generating alternatives, prototyping, comparing approaches and exposing unfamiliar possibilities.</p>
        <p>But once something becomes important enough to rely on, the standard changes. Critical decisions and systems should become understandable, testable and maintainable by the people responsible for them.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Use AI to explore widely. Build understanding around what survives.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Current experiment</p>
        <h2>Does the Cognitive Kernel improve real work?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The next experiment compares matched real tasks with and without the current Cognitive Kernel guidance.</p>
        <p>It looks at practical outcomes such as human time, whether the work is actually completed, later rework, mistakes and whether the person can still explain or defend the important decisions.</p>
        <p class="large">The point is to measure consequences, not whether a prompt sounds sensible.</p>
        <p><a href="/projects/">See the current project state →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">A simple loop</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>How the practice works.</h2>
          <p>This is a working method, not a claim that the method has already been proven generally.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {steps.map(([title, copy], i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{title}</h3>
              <p>{copy}</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">When something works</p>
        <h2>Turn useful lessons into things others can use.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>A successful experiment might produce a better way of working, a reusable tool, a research result, a teaching method or simply stronger human capability.</p>
        <p>Not every useful outcome needs a new theory or publication. The important question is whether something worthwhile became easier to understand or do.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
